What your logs tell us
Every batch is exactly:



Kafka Records : 10000
for batches 0-9.

That means Spark is hitting your limit:



MAX_OFFSETS_PER_TRIGGER = "10000"
So Spark is continuously reading the maximum allowed messages each trigger.

Why Spark is falling behind
You have:



TRIGGER_INTERVAL = "5 second"
but processing:



10000 records
takes:



17s - 46s
per batch.

For example:



Batch 0
Records = 10000
Time = 46.6 sec


