Even the smallest batch is taking longer than 5 seconds.

The real reason
Your producer generates:



130 messages/sec
A 5-second trigger only needs to process:



130 × 5
=
650 messages
Yet Spark is processing:



10000 messages
per batch because there is a backlog in Kafka.

First fix
Change:



MAX_OFFSETS_PER_TRIGGER = "10000"
to:



MAX_OFFSETS_PER_TRIGGER = "1000"
or even:



MAX_OFFSETS_PER_TRIGGER = "500"
Second fix
Change:



STARTING_OFFSETS = "earliest"
to:



STARTING_OFFSETS = "latest"
for testing.

With earliest, Spark consumes all historical Kafka data.

With latest, Spark starts from current messages only.

Third fix
Increase trigger interval:



TRIGGER_INTERVAL = "15 seconds"
or



TRIGGER_INTERVAL = "30 seconds"
A good combination for your workload:



STARTING_OFFSETS = "latest"
MAX_OFFSETS_PER_TRIGGER = "1000"
TRIGGER_INTERVAL = "15 seconds"
