If Spark is mandatory because you're building a Kafka → Bronze → Silver → Gold lakehouse pipeline, tune Spark (latest, 100 offsets, local[*], remove counts).
If the goal is simply "every stock tick must be processed within 2 seconds", then use a dedicated Kafka consumer for Silver ingestion and keep Spark for downstream processing only. That will easily satisfy your latency requirement.






